glacis.d:
n. A gentle slope, or a smooth, gently sloping bank;
   especially (Fort.), that slope of earth which inclines from the covered
   way toward the exterior ground or country (see Illust. of Ravelin).

glossology.d:
n. The definition and explanation of terms; a glossary.
n. The science of language; comparative philology;
   linguistics; glottology.

goldylocks.d:
n. A plant of several species of the genus Chrysocoma; --
   so called from the tufts of yellow flowers which terminate the stems;
   also, the Ranunculus auricomus, a kind of buttercup.

grabble.d:
v. i. To grope; to feel with the hands.
v. i. To lie prostrate on the belly; to sprawl on the ground;
   to grovel.

grisettes.d:
plural of grisette
n. A French girl or young married woman of the lower class;
   more frequently, a young working woman who is fond of gallantry.

gypsyism.d:
n. The arts and practices or habits of gypsies; deception;
   cheating; flattery.
n. The state of a gypsy.
